fact WorkItem(id: "WI-093", description: some(value: "Time stdlib (anthill.prelude.time): minimal time vocabulary needed for simulation, scheduling, and impurity reasoning. Three pieces. (1) Tick effect — sort Tick with fact Effect[T = Tick]. Operations marked 'effects Tick' depend on or advance simulation/wall-clock time; two calls separated by a Tick are not interchangeable. (2) Clock resource — sort Clock with entity clock, plus operations: now(c: Clock) -> Timestamp effects Tick; advance(c: Clock, by: Duration) -> Unit effects {Modify[c], Tick}. (3) Arithmetic on existing Duration / Timestamp data shapes from primitives.anthill — addition, subtraction, comparison, Numeric and Ordered satisfaction facts as appropriate. Driver: lf1 webots example wants Design B effect modeling — sensor reads stay pure (referentially transparent within a tick, matching webots's contract that sensor values update only via Robot::step), and Robot::step is the only Tick-emitting op. Without a Tick effect we can't express this, so all impurity is currently flattened into Modify. Connected to safety.anthill's inductive_invariant which already reasons in discrete steps; Tick on step makes the proof transition explicit. Out of scope: real-time / wall-clock semantics, time zones, scheduling primitives — those are separate stdlib chunks once concrete consumers appear."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
